// ModelSwapper cvars.

// CONFIG VERSION. Bumped whenever a shipped DEFAULT changes, so an existing
// ini picks the change up instead of silently overriding it -- an archived
// server cvar always beats this file. See RS_ForeignModelHandler.MigrateConfig,
// which applies the change once and stamps this.
//
//   0 -- never migrated. A fresh install starts here, already holds the
//        current defaults from below, and is stamped on first load.
//   1 -- rs_foreignmodels_byfamily defaults off.
server int rs_fm_cfgver = 0;

server bool rs_foreignmodels         = true;   // master switch
server bool rs_foreignmodels_dump    = false;  // dump the scan to console
server bool rs_foreignmodels_showall = false;  // include weapons with no slot binding

// (rs_foreignmodels_natural and rs_fm_learned are gone: the remap engine
// reads timing off the weapon's own state table every tic, so there is
// no learned timing to store and no "natural rate" distinct from theirs.
// A stale archived copy in an old ini is ignored harmlessly.)

// The player's own model choices, packed as class:archetype:pick1:pick2;...
// Written every time a pick changes. Keyed on class name only -- no notion
// of "which mod" anywhere -- which is what makes this work as a per-mod
// profile with nothing tracking which mod is loaded: only one mod's classes
// exist in the world at a time. Clear it with the menu.
server string rs_fm_picks = "";

// THEIR CASINGS COME OUT OF YOUR FACE. A weapon mod spawns brass, smoke
// and ejection effects relative to the PLAYER, because on a monitor the
// player and the gun are the same place. In a headset they are not: the
// gun is in a tracked hand and the eye is your face, so the brass leaves
// your cheekbone and swings around as you look up and down.
//
// This shifts anything a mod spawns next to the eye, in the moment after
// you work the weapon, by the vector from the eye to the muzzle. It
// TRANSLATES rather than repositions, so every offset and every velocity
// the author wrote survives intact -- the ejection arc is the one they
// drew, starting from the gun instead of your face.
//
// Only for weapons wearing one of our models, because we are the reason
// the gun moved. On by default: the displacement it corrects is one this
// mod causes.
server bool rs_fm_effects = true;

// Extra distance from the grip to the muzzle, on top of the per-family
// figure. The engine has no muzzle concept -- a weapon acts from the
// hand -- so this is where the casing relocator aims its shift.
server int rs_fm_muzzle = 0;   // map units, clamped -20..80

// Collapse the picker to ONE ROW PER FAMILY -- one shotgun row, one smg row.
//
// OFF by default. The picker exists to show the weapons the scan actually
// found, by name, and let you put a model on each one. A row labelled
// "all shotgun" answers a question nobody asked first.
//
// Turn it ON when a mod's class count makes that unworkable: Brutal Doom 22
// shows 85 rows, DoomRL Arsenal about 150, and across the test corpus there
// are 934 weapon classes of which only 276 even declare a slot. Most of
// those rows are the same gun in a different mode -- BrutalPistol,
// DualPistols and PuristPistol are all your pistol -- and one row per
// family is the escape hatch for exactly that case.
server bool rs_foreignmodels_byfamily = false;

// Show only weapons you are CARRYING. The cheapest honest filter there is:
// a mod can invent classes without limit, but you only ever hold the ones
// your player class was given. Guncaster and Trailblazer name their weapons
// Brimstone and Bitchmaker -- no token list will ever classify those, and no
// filter built on names will ever shorten that menu. Your inventory answers
// both questions without asking the mod anything.
//
// Off by default: a player who wants to dress a gun before finding it should
// meet the whole list first.
server bool rs_foreignmodels_carried = false;

// Offer models even when a weapon already has one of its own.
//
// ON by default, because the flag we can read cannot answer the question we
// actually have. Actor.hasmodel means "this class has a model bound to SOME
// sprite" -- it says nothing about WHICH. A mod that models its dropped
// pickup and leaves the first-person view as flat sprites reads identically
// to one that ships full HUD models.
//
// Project Brutality is exactly that mod. Its MODELDEF binds sprite VIFL and
// its Spawn state runs A_PBVPFramework -- the pickup lying on the floor. Its
// Fire states use R0F8 and have no model at all. hasmodel came back true, we
// stood down, and we withheld models from the weapons that most needed them.
//
// Pickup models are common; first-person weapon models are rare -- a mod
// that had them would not need this one. So offering is the right default.
// Turn this off to leave any modelled weapon alone.
server bool rs_foreignmodels_replaceown = true;

// ===========================================================================
// QUEST BUILD ONLY. build.ps1 -Static ships this file in place of the root
// lump of the same name; the desktop build never sees it. Added 2026-10-24
// for the VR reload / hands / melee code brought in from the RSQ Weapon
// Depot runtime, which is QuestZDoom 17.3 code. The REMA version is separate.
// ===========================================================================

// ---- CVARINFO.rsvr ----
// RS VR melee (zscript/rsvr/melee.zs): the axe and the Dragonslayer.

// How hard a swing has to be before the blade cuts. 1.0 is the shipped feel; higher asks for a
// harder swing, lower cuts on less. Multiplies the per-weapon threshold.
user float rsvr_melee_swing = 1.0;
// How much of the blade's motion must point DOWN for a swing to cut: 0.25 is about 15 degrees
// below level (owner, 2026-10-16: only a meaningful downward swing cuts; never level, never up).
user float rsvr_melee_down = 0.25;

// What you HOLD to ready the axe throw, as a usercmd button mask. Default 16 = BT_ALTATTACK,
// which is how it has always worked. QuestZDoom has no usercmd bit for the weapon hand's grip,
// so to throw on the grip either bind the grip to one of the engine's user buttons and set this
// to it (BT_USER1 2097152, BT_USER2 4194304, BT_USER3 8388608, BT_USER4 16777216), or put the
// grip's raw key codes in rsvr_axe_keys below. 0 = never hold, so the throw is off.
user int rsvr_axe_hold = 16;
// Raw key codes that also ready the throw, space separated, read the way rsr_grip_keys is.
// Empty by default. Turn on Print each reload step (rsr_debug) and press your grip to read its
// code, then put it here.
user string rsvr_axe_keys = "";

// Two-handed axe: how squarely the cutting edge must lead the swing before the second
// hand is worth anything. 0.5 is about 60 degrees off the edge; 1.0 demands a perfect
// edge-on blow, 0 pays for any direction. The axe is bladed on one side, so holding it
// with both hands is not the reward -- landing the edge is (owner, 2026-10-23).
user float rsvr_axe_edge = 0.5;

// Axe lock-on (one-handed throw). Hold the throw and the axe paints the monster your
// hand is pointing at; release into the throw and it goes there. The cone is how far
// off your aim a target may be to be picked up; a lock already made is kept out to
// a little over twice that before it drops, so it does not flicker as you wind up.
user float rsvr_axe_lock_cone = 16.0;
user float rsvr_axe_lock_range = 1200.0;

// ---- CVARINFO.rsq ----
// RS VR hands / reload / ballistics. Options: RSQ_Options in MENUDEF.rsq. v9.
user bool rsq_hands = true;			// VR hands on the controllers
user int rsr_reload = 1;			// Reloading: 1 VR (zscript/rsr, on the guns that have it; the rest stock), 0 stock
server bool rsq_ballistics = false;	// enhanced impacts and projectile trails (server: they use playsim random)
user int rsq_punch = 0;			// VR punching: a real punch with either fist lands (zscript/rsq/fists.zs)
// 2026-10-23: a punch that lands on a switch or any usable line works it, at the fist's own reach
// instead of the engine's 64-unit use range. The LINE'S SPECIAL decides, not its texture.
user bool rsq_punch_use = true;
server bool rsq_extra_weapons = false;	// cheats also give the MP40, MG42, Devastator, Hellish launcher, flame cannon (zscript/nosniper)
user int rsr_grab_with = 0;		// 1.17 Grab ammo with: 0 off trigger, 1 off grip (1.14 rule), 2 Use key (only while a reload has the hand)
user bool rsq_flick = true;		// 1.17 Flick to reload: a gun in each hand, snap a barrel down to reload that gun (zscript/rsq/flick.zs)
// 2026-10-23: the VR scopes (zscript/rsq/scope.zs). Per gun, 0 DOT (a collimated red dot on
// the gun's own glass, no magnification) or 1 REAL (the view down the bore rendered into it).
// RSQ_ScopeTable.ModeCVar() maps the table index to these names, so a new scoped gun needs a
// row in that table and a cvar here and nothing else.
user int rsq_scope_sniper = 0;
user int rsq_scope_railgun = 0;

// ---- CVARINFO.rsr ----
// RS real VR reload (zscript/rsr/vreload.zs). rsr_reload 1 (CVARINFO.rsq) turns it on for the guns that have it.
user string rsr_grip_keys = "443 436";	// key codes that are the off-hand grip (it grabs only 50 cm or more from the gun hand, or with vr_two_handed_weapons 0): 443 KEY_PAD_RTHUMB, 436 KEY_PAD_DPAD_UP (with the main grip held as a shift)
user int rsr_grab_buttons = 67108864;	// usercmd buttons that grab anywhere: BT_OFFHANDATTACK (off-hand trigger); 0 = none
user int rsr_magrelease = 268435456;	// usercmd buttons that drop the magazine: BT_OFFHANDRELOAD; the gun's own reload always does
user int rsr_pouch = 0;				// where a new magazine is taken: 0 anywhere 20 cm from the gun, 1 low (40 cm below the eyes)
user bool rsr_eat_grip = true;		// while a reload has the off hand, its grip key does nothing else (rthumb is +speed in some layouts)
user bool ms_mod_first = true;	// the mod's reload runs at the press, the gun holds its fire until the hands finish; off: held first, the mod's reload after
user bool ms_off_fist = true;	// the off hand is these hands (the fists) unless a gun is moved there; off: a mod's own off-hand weapon stays
user bool ms_hand_pump = true;	// pump a foreign shotgun by hand after each shot (off: the mod pumps by itself)
user bool ms_charge_dry = true;	// a gun reloaded from empty asks for its charging handle (off: the magazine is the whole reload)
user int ms_reload_sounds = 1;	// 1 ModelSwapper's reload foley while the hands work, 0 the loaded mod's sounds only
user bool rsr_debug = false;		// print every key code pressed, and each reload step

// 1.93: take the charging handle / slide with no reload running, so the action can be cracked
// open on a loaded gun and let go again (a press check). A look, not a rack: no ammo moves and
// nothing chambers. Needs "Grab ammo with" set to the trigger or the grip, because the Use key
// is only taken over while a reload has the off hand.
user bool rsr_freecharge = false;

// Reload assist (zscript/rsr/rsr_assist.zs): one number scales every capture radius and
// tolerance of the real VR reload at once, and how little of a push or a stroke counts as
// done. 1.0 is the shipped feel; 0.5 asks for the old precision; 3.0 is very forgiving.
user float rsr_assist = 1.0;
// Draw the capture zones as rings. A tuning aid, not a play feature -- but it IS in the menu
// (Reload: tuning and debug), because a console command is no use with a headset on. With it
// off not one particle is spawned, and these are particles, never actors, so nothing becomes
// a marker in the world.
user bool rsr_assist_debug = false;

// Pump shotguns: how many shells one pushed home counts as, 1 to 4. The reserve pays for every
// one of them; this only saves you inserting eight times to fill a tube.
user int rsr_shell_credit = 1;

// 1.30 the rifle's M203 (zscript/rsr/rsr_m203.zs): what a hand-loaded round costs. 0 a rocket (as
// BD22's own launcher reload), 1 a hand grenade. A server setting: it changes what you have.
server int rsm_ammo = 0;

// 1.37 secondary fire on the zoom buttons (zscript/rsq/alts.zs): off = BD22 as it was
server bool rsa_pistol_semi = false;	// pistol: one shot per trigger pull
server bool rsa_rev_magnum = false;	// revolver: secondary fires a slug
server bool rsa_sg_slug = false;		// pump shotgun: secondary fires a slug

// SERVER, not user. A `user` cvar is per player and has to be read against one;
// DonorInHand is `clearscope static` and has no player to read against. The Depot
// hit this exact wall and wrote it down (bd22_plus.py, rsb_revolver_feed): "Server,
// not user: Index() is clearscope static with no player to read a user cvar against."
// It is also the right scope on its own terms -- which reload runs is playsim state,
// not a per-player preference, so every peer must agree on it.
server string ms_donor_main = "";
server string ms_donor_off = "";

// The join's trace: one line per state change on a weapon that HAS a reload slot,
// saying whether the remap was found and which labelled group its state is in.
// Off by default; a join that silently declines looks exactly like a gun that is
// simply not reloading, which is the hardest kind of bug to see.
server int ms_join_trace = 0;
